  "result": "```js\nasync function getUser(id) {\n  const rows = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);\n  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');\n  return rows[0];\n}\n```\n\nKey changes:\n- `async` function replaces the `callback` parameter\n- `await` replaces the nested callback \u2014 errors from `db.query` propagate automatically as rejections\n- Explicit error check becomes a thrown error, which callers handle with `try/catch` or `.catch()`\n\nCallers update from `getUser(id, (err, user) => ...)` to:\n```js\n// async/await\nconst user = await getUser(id);\n\n// or promise-style\ngetUser(id).then(user => ...).catch(err => ...);\n```\n\nThis assumes `db.query` returns a promise \u2014 if it's still callback-based, wrap it first with `util.promisify(db.query.bind(db))`.",
